2026-10-26T13:09:28.7284097Z error[vulnerability]: Buffered application data sent to outer server after ECH rejection
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7285636Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/spotuify/spotuify/Cargo.lock:368:1
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7286421Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7287042Z 368 │ rustls 0.23.45 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7288076Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7288703Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7289009Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0347
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7289562Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0347
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7290335Z     ├ When a server rejects Encrypted Client Hello (ECH), the client completes the
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7291035Z       handshake using the outer ClientHello and authenticates the server against the
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7291689Z       ECH config's `public_name`. At the end of that handshake, rustls encrypted and
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7297558Z       queued any application data buffered via `ClientConnection::writer()` *before*
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7298150Z       queueing the `ech_required` alert.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7298471Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7298721Z       The application correctly receives
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7299575Z       `Error::PeerIncompatible(ServerRejectedEncryptedClientHello)`, but the next
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7300286Z       `write_tls()` call (needed to send the alert) also sends the buffered
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7300906Z       application data. Plaintext meant for the inner server therefore goes to the
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7301451Z       client-facing server named by `public_name`.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7302044Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7302528Z       That server is authenticated, so this is not exploitable by an unauthenticated
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7303166Z       party, but it violates RFC 9849 section 6.1.6, which requires the client to
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7303790Z       abort with `ech_required` "before sending any application data to the server".
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7304262Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7304501Z       This affects only clients that:
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7304808Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7305135Z       - use `EchMode::Enable` (GREASE ECH is not affected),
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7305655Z       - write application data before the handshake completes, and
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7306483Z       - connect to a server that rejects their ECH config (for example, because it is stale).
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7307007Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7307421Z       The underlying ordering bug is older, but before 0.23.44 the client checked
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7308089Z       the server certificate against the inner server name rather than `public_name`,
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7308704Z       so certificate verification failed first and no data was sent.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7309471Z     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/pull/3300
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7310162Z     ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.46 (try `cargo update -p rustls`)
