2026-10-26T13:09:28.7334619Z error[vulnerability]: Brotli certificate decompression can allocate up to 1 GiB before authentication
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7335440Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/spotuify/spotuify/Cargo.lock:368:1
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7335903Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7336581Z 368 │ rustls 0.23.45 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7337601Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7338221Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7338526Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0348
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7339029Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0348
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7339747Z     ├ The built-in Brotli certificate decompressor (enabled by the non-default
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7340418Z       `brotli` crate feature) bounded the size of the decompressed output, but
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7340973Z       accepted a peer-selected history window. Brotli's large-window extension was
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7341496Z       enabled, so a five-byte header could cause an allocation of 1 GiB. A peer can
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7342442Z       abort a process whose allocator cannot satisfy that request.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7342841Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7343223Z       No trusted certificate is required by the attacker. Affected configurations are:
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7343653Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7343986Z       - clients that enable the `brotli` feature and connect to a malicious server, and
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7344543Z       - servers that enable the `brotli` feature and request client certificates.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7344930Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7345267Z       Applications that do not enable the `brotli` feature are not affected.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7345865Z     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/pull/3297
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7346457Z     ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.46 (try `cargo update -p rustls`)
