2026-10-26T13:09:28.7366593Z error[vulnerability]: Unauthenticated ServerHello can downgrade later connections to classical key exchange
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7367360Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/spotuify/spotuify/Cargo.lock:368:1
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7368031Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7368604Z 368 │ rustls 0.23.45 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7369525Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7370070Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7370357Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0349
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7370818Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0349
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7371468Z     ├ The client recorded the server-selected key exchange group for each server
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7372200Z       name when processing the ServerHello, before the server was authenticated.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7372743Z       This record is used to predict which key share to send in future ClientHellos
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7373183Z       to that server name.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7373435Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7373770Z       A network attacker can answer one connection attempt with a ServerHello
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7374359Z       selecting X25519, and then close the connection. Later ClientHellos for that
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7374892Z       name carry only an X25519 key share, while `supported_groups` still lists
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7375431Z       X25519MLKEM768 first. If the genuine server accepts that share rather than
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7375979Z       sending a HelloRetryRequest for its preferred hybrid group, the handshake
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7376543Z       completes with classical-only key exchange and no error. This persists for as
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7377058Z       long as the entry stays in the client's session store.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7377379Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7377733Z       The impact is loss of post-quantum confidentiality for affected connections
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7378265Z       ("harvest now, decrypt later"). There is no key compromise and no
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7378872Z       authentication bypass.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7379147Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7379358Z       The following are not affected:
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7379620Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7379989Z       - connections to servers which send a HelloRetryRequest for their preferred group,
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7380561Z       - clients with resumption disabled (as nothing is stored), and
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7380955Z       - other server names.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7381189Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7381404Z       This behaviour is discussed in
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7382447Z       [draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction](https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-tls-key-share-prediction-01.html#name-security-considerations),
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7383296Z       so the practical impact depends largely on server policy.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7383873Z     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/rustls/rustls/pull/3355
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7384510Z     ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=0.23.46 (try `cargo update -p rustls`)
