2026-10-26T13:09:28.7453932Z error[unsound]: `AsyncFd::new` and related constructors violate I/O safety
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7454527Z     ┌─ /home/runner/work/spotuify/spotuify/Cargo.lock:475:1
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7455064Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7455565Z 475 │ tokio 1.52.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7456329Z     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ unsound advisory detected
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7456788Z     │
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7457053Z     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0386
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7457473Z     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0386
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7459430Z     ├ `tokio::io::unix::AsyncFd` provides safe constructors (`new`, `with_interest`, `try_new`, and `try_with_interest`) that accept any `T: AsRawFd` rather than requiring proof of ownership or validity of the file descriptor. Because `RawFd` implements `AsRawFd`, safe code can construct an `AsyncFd` from an arbitrary or closed file descriptor, or close/replace the underlying file descriptor while the `AsyncFd` is still alive.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7461123Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7461330Z       This violates I/O safety in two ways:
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7461595Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7462623Z       1. `AsyncFd<T>` implements `AsFd` for all `T: AsRawFd` by calling `BorrowedFd::borrow_raw(self.as_raw_fd())`, allowing safe code to obtain an arbitrary `BorrowedFd<'_>` without owning the file descriptor.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7465041Z       2. Tokio's I/O driver stores a pointer to an internal allocation in the `epoll`/`kqueue` user data for registered file descriptors. If the underlying file descriptor is duplicated and then closed while an `AsyncFd` is alive, and the OS reuses that file descriptor number for a another IO resource on the same runtime, dropping the first `AsyncFd` deregisters the reused file descriptor number and frees the first while the original file description remains registered in `epoll`, leading to a use-after-free when a readiness event fires.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7466927Z
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7468164Z       Starting in Tokio 1.51.6, 1.53.3, and 1.54.0, `AsyncFd::new`, `AsyncFd::with_interest`, `AsyncFd::try_new`, and `AsyncFd::try_with_interest` are deprecated in favor of the `unsafe` constructors `AsyncFd::register` and `AsyncFd::register_with_interest`. Callers must ensure that the file descriptor remains valid, open, and unchanged for the lifetime of the `AsyncFd`.
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7469648Z     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio/pull/8587
2026-10-26T13:09:28.7470232Z     ├ Solution: Upgrade to >=1.51.6, <1.52.0 OR >=1.53.3 (try `cargo update -p tokio`)
